.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-pr-watch 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-pr\-watch \- Poll a head\*(Aqs check runs until the required set answers, then report the verdict
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten pr watch\fR [\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-absent\-ok\fR] [\fB\-\-fanin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-sha\fR> <\fB\-\-required\fR> <\fB\-\-answered\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Poll a head\*(Aqs check runs until the required set answers, then report the verdict
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-sha\fR \fI<sha>\fR
The commit whose check runs to read
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<repo>\fR
The repository to read, in the forge client\*(Aqs own spelling
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<interval>\fR
Seconds between requests; a server\-requested floor raises it and nothing lowers it
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<progress>\fR
Program to record the poll\*(Aqs tick and reading\-change signals
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\-id\fR \fI<progress_id>\fR
The identity the progress recorder keys its entries on
.TP
\fB\-\-required\fR \fI<required>\fR
Comma\-separated check names that carry a verdict about this repository
.TP
\fB\-\-absent\-ok\fR \fI<absent_ok>\fR
Comma\-separated check names for which having no run at all is a legitimate reading
.TP
\fB\-\-answered\fR \fI<answered>\fR
Comma\-separated conclusions that constitute an answer; anything else is not yet one
.TP
\fB\-\-fanin\fR \fI<fanin>\fR
The fan\-in check whose failure a cancelled sibling can manufacture
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
